laurel 2987: after a watchdog bark the bite stays armed through the panic hold, so a stuck CPU ends in a reset, with no key press.

[V 2026-11-03 17:56:16, kernel 833d75cdc9] A bark on a stuck CPU 5 sent its report and printed `LAUREL PANIC: holding`, then the hold gave no pong and took no `ctl bootloader`; 2986 had stopped the hardware for the hold, so only the Power key could end it. Now: a bark panic keeps the 30 s count of laurel_wdog_panic_begin. Any other panic holds as before. Kill switch: laurelwdog=0 (2986).

